      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is still relevant, probably more so now because players can move their own audio listener with drones and stream cameras.\n\nIt would be extremely easy for someone to leave a stream camera just outside the walls of a room and enable the 'Audio from Camera' toggle from another location. Unless you poke your head through all the walls to find the lens, it's currently impossible to know someone else is listening.\n\nIt still does upset me that the ability to see who's receiving your voice audio was removed simply because the main menu got updated.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-08T01:08:35.026Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The Ear icon in the Social menu's \"In Room\" section was left out of the new menu. This icon would let you know if you were in someone else's hearing range, and was occasionally very helpful to figure out if someone was spying or could otherwise hear a conversation that was meant to be private.",
